# MLOps Style Rules

## Type Hints (mandatory)
- All public functions: full type hints including return type.
- DataFrames: `pd.DataFrame` with column names documented in docstring.
- MLflow run IDs: `str`. Model versions: `int`. Stages: `Literal["Staging", "Production", "Archived"]`.

## Naming Conventions
- Training scripts: `train_{model_type}.py` (e.g., `train_xgboost.py`)
- Feature functions: `compute_{feature_group}(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame`
- Metric functions: `evaluate_{metric}(y_true, y_pred) -> float`
- MLflow experiment: `{project_name}/{model_family}` — no spaces, lowercase, hyphens
- Model registry name: `{project_name}-{target}` (e.g., `churn-30day`, `fraud-transaction`)

## MLflow Logging Discipline
- Log ALL hyperparameters at run start: `mlflow.log_params(params_dict)`
- Log metrics at end with step if time-series: `mlflow.log_metric("val_auc", auc, step=epoch)`
- Log model with signature: always pass `input_example` to `mlflow.sklearn.log_model()` so the registry auto-infers schema
- Use tags for non-numeric metadata: `mlflow.set_tags({"data_version": "v3", "triggered_by": "ci"})`

## No Magic Numbers
- All thresholds (accuracy floor, latency SLA, drift threshold) live in `shared/config.py` as pydantic-settings fields with env var overrides.
- Never hard-code `if accuracy > 0.85` — use `if accuracy > settings.min_accuracy_threshold`.

## Reproducibility Checklist (enforced in pipeline.py)
```python
# Every training run must:
mlflow.log_param("random_seed", SEED)
mlflow.log_param("data_hash", compute_data_hash(df))
mlflow.log_artifact("requirements.txt")
mlflow.set_tag("git_commit", subprocess.check_output(["git", "rev-parse", "HEAD"]).decode().strip())
```
